pears above","second TF AC: 'the threshold and warning changes'"],"finding":"The acceptance criteria reference a 'warning' value (AC 'bedrock_spend_cap.tf carries the threshold and warning values derived above' and the terraform-plan AC 'the threshold and warning changes') but the Figures section derives only the intended cap, CEILING and threshold — the warning value has no stated derivation or definition.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"fed61ac2119a615ba","impact":1.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"Figures section vs AC 'bedrock_spend_cap.tf carries the threshold and warning values derived above'","norm_id":"n11a97ddbbda2fd8d","priority":1.0,"reason":"high-priority+criterion-opted-in","recalled":false,"scenarios":["Executor reaches the tf AC and cannot compute the warning value because no formula is given"],"severity":null,"suggested_fix":"Add a Figures bullet defining the warning value (e.g. 'warning: N% of threshold') alongside the threshold derivation.","tier":"LLM","validity":1.0,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"yes","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"yes","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"yes","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"yes"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"missing_oracle","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"low","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"uncertifiable_outcome","internal_conflict":"medium","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"high","prod_impact":"low","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"self_revealing","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"high"}}},{"block_threshold":0.7,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"- [ ] State how `_ce_spend_today` builds its Cost Explorer request after `BEDROCK_SERVICE_VALUES` is deleted — either an unfiltered GROUP_BY SERVICE query filtered by the new predicate, or a derived value list — since the allowlist currently supplies the request's `Filter.Dimensions.Values`.","cohort":["G1G2"],"criteria":["G1G2"],"decision":"block","decision_margin":0.1889,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["handler.py line 486: `\"Filter\": {\"Dimensions\": {\"Key\": \"SERVICE\", \"Values\": BEDROCK_SERVICE_VALUES}}` inside `_ce_spend_today`","AC line: '`BEDROCK_SERVICE_VALUES`... are absent' deletes the symbol","AC line: '`_ce_spend_today` classifies by predicate — service equals `Amazon Bedrock` or ends with the Bedrock Edition suffix' describes result classification, not the CE request filter"],"finding":"The plan deletes BEDROCK_SERVICE_VALUES but does not specify how _ce_spend_today's Cost Explorer request is filtered afterward. That allowlist is currently the Filter.Dimensions.Values list in the get_cost_and_usage request (handler.py line 486); a predicate can classify returned groups but the CE request itself still needs an explicit SERVICE value list or must be re-issued unfiltered and grouped by SERVICE. The AC re-specs classification of results without addressing the request-side filter that the deleted symbol supplied.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f09bd67f345e4359a","impact":1.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"Acceptance Criteria: '_ce_spend_today classifies by predicate...' and '...BEDROCK_SERVICE_VALUES... are absent'","norm_id":"n34e61a445061cc72","priority":0.8889,"reason":"high-priority+criterion-opted-in","recalled":false,"scenarios":["Implementer removes BEDROCK_SERVICE_VALUES and leaves the CE request referencing the deleted name, or silently drops the SERVICE filter and pulls all-service spend"],"severity":null,"suggested_fix":"","tier":"LLM","validity":0.8889,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"yes","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"no","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"yes","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"no","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"yes"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"underspecified_oracle","blast_radius":"module","debt_impact":"low","divergent_implementation":"omits_required_site","dod_uncertifiable":"underspecified_certification","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"medium","prod_impact":"medium","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"self_revealing","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"medium"}}},{"block_threshold":0.6,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Resolve the shared-threshold defect so the ceiling over-price compensation does not delay the CE arm: either apply the ratio R only to the metered ceiling estimate before max() (compare max(ceiling_estimate/R, ce_spend) against the unscaled cap), or carry two thresholds so ce_spend is enforced against the intended cap and the ceiling estimate against the scaled one.","cohort":["G6"],"criteria":["G6"],"decision":"block","decision_margin":0.2889,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["The threshold-scaling median ratio R = (undimensioned tokens x CEILING)/(CE Bedrock total) is >= 1 because ceiling pricing over-estimates (plan states 'Ceiling pricing over-estimates cheap models').","handler.py line 664/718 compares the effective spend (which may be ce_spend, real dollars) against THRESHOLD_USD; if THRESHOLD_USD is raised to cap*R, the CE arm trips only at cap*R real dollars.","Plan thesis: 'so the estimate is an upper bound and the cap cannot fire late' — the scaled shared threshold reintroduces late firing on the CE arm."],"finding":"Scaling the single THRESHOLD_USD up by the ceiling/CE median ratio R (>=1) while comparing max(ceiling_estimate, ce_spend) against it degrades the CE enforcement arm: because ce_spend is real billed dollars, the CE arm now only trips at cap*R real dollars instead of the intended cap, so the authoritative signal fires LATE — the very failure mode the story exists to eliminate.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"fd5de57718a3d2ea7","impact":1.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"Figures ('threshold: the intended daily cap scaled by the median of (undimensioned tokens x CEILING) / (CE Bedrock total)') and AC 'Enforcement compares max(ceiling_estimate, ce_spend)'","norm_id":"na7f1b6f56add5306","priority":0.8889,"reason":"high-priority+criterion-opted-in","recalled":false,"scenarios":["A model that meters no token metric (batch/provisioned throughput) so only CE covers it: CE reaches the intended cap in real dollars but does not trip until cap*R.","R materially above 1 (embedding-heavy or cache-heavy days) widening the gap between intended and effective CE cap."],"severity":null,"suggested_fix":"Divide the ceiling estimate by the median ratio (or equivalently keep the metered arm's own scaled threshold) so that ce_spend continues to be compared against the unscaled var.bedrock_daily_cap_usd, preserving the intended dollar cap on the authoritative signal.","tier":"LLM","validity":0.8889,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"na","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"no","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"yes","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"yes","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"no","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"yes"},"severity_attributes":{"